.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt TRX_STRERROR 3
.Os @PACKAGE_STRING@
.Sh NAME
.Nm trx_strerror
.Nd describe a status code
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In trivnote/trx.h
.Ft const char *
.Fn trx_strerror "int status"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn trx_strerror
function returns a static, human-readable description of a status
code.
The status codes are:
.Bl -tag -width ".Dv TRX_ENOMEM"
.It Dv TRX_OK
Success (0).
.It Dv TRX_EOF
End of input.
.It Dv TRX_ENOMEM
An allocation failed.
.It Dv TRX_EIO
The read callback reported an error.
.It Dv TRX_EBAD
The input is malformed.
.It Dv TRX_ENOSYS
Not implemented yet.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn trx_strerror
function returns a string that must not be modified or freed.
An unrecognised code yields
.Qq unknown status .
